      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the weight of one bowling ball given that the weights of the bowling balls and canoes follow the specified ratio and that two canoes weigh a total of 56 pounds.\n\nLet's denote the weight of one bowling ball as \\( B \\) and the weight of one canoe as \\( C \\). According to the problem, seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes. This can be written as:\n\n\\[ 7B = 3C \\]\n\nWe are also given that two canoes weigh a total of 56 pounds. This can be written as:\n\n\\[ 2C = 56 \\]\n\nFrom the second equation, we can solve for \\( C \\):\n\n\\[ C = \\frac{56}{2} = 28 \\]\n\nNow that we know the weight of one canoe is 28 pounds, we can substitute \\( C = 28 \\) into the first equation:\n\n\\[ 7B = 3 \\times 28 \\]\n\\[ 7B = 84 \\]\n\nTo find the weight of one bowling ball, we solve for \\( B \\):\n\n\\[ B = \\frac{84}{7} = 12 \\]\n\nTherefore, the weight of one bowling ball is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) pounds.",
