    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the weight of one bowling ball, we start by defining the variables for the weights of the bowling balls and the canoes. Let \\( b \\) represent the weight of one bowling ball in pounds, and \\( c \\) represent the weight of one canoe in pounds.\n\nAccording to the problem, seven identical bowling balls weigh the same as three identical canoes. This relationship can be expressed with the equation:\n\\[ 7b = 3c \\]\n\nWe are also given that two canoes weigh a total of 56 pounds. This can be written as:\n\\[ 2c = 56 \\]\n\nTo find the value of \\( c \\), we solve the second equation:\n\\[ c = \\frac{56}{2} = 28 \\]\n\nNow that we know the weight of one canoe is 28 pounds, we substitute \\( c = 28 \\) into the first equation:\n\\[ 7b = 3 \\times 28 \\]\n\\[ 7b = 84 \\]\n\nTo find the weight of one bowling ball, we solve for \\( b \\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 7:\n\\[ b = \\frac{84}{7} = 12 \\]\n\nTherefore, the weight of one bowling ball is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) pounds.",
